"""Mutations of part 8d-iii's decorators code (src/game/decorators.cpp from GetMinSlope on: the
light map, the models taken and given back, the animated meshes, the grid's refills and moves, the
bends around the soldier and the cars, the bends' update, the sway) for ../mutfast.py with the world
build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_8d3.py --models DIR --build build_world.bat --check check_world.py

DIR holds a .txt per mission ("mission NAME"; the tests run the same in each). Each mutation should
make check_world.py fail (or the harness crash / hang). Generated from the 8d-iii lines only (a
comparison, a number, an operator or a statement per line), then pruned. The expected Follow
refills come from a model of the original's code (_re/tools/decorator_follow_sim.py). Left out as
equivalent (68):
- Follow: dx / dz >= 0, <= 0, < 1 inside the moved branches (dx / dz are not 0 there); n >= / <=
  the sub index (an empty loop, the same value stored); the return after a reset (the fresh cells
  would bend in the same update, not the next: not seen, a reset clears them first).
- Exact float ties that cannot occur: squares at exactly 1e-8, |target| at the double degree,
  the alpha or light exactly at its clamp; the normalizations' unit test with sq + 1 (never under
  1e-8: a unit vector times 1 is itself).
- Scale only: a direction's normalization (its 1 / sqrt as 1.5, its square summed with a
  difference) where only atan2 or the sign reads it (the bend's facing, the soldier's move); the
  wheel's 1.5 unit test (its square is far from 1.5 in play and the 1.5 case is tested).
- The axis' y (always 0 in PrepareAnimated); the slope's (z + x) * 0; the refill's initial
  random rotation / height (TakeModel sets them); a new bend's angle 0 (already).
- Sign tests of a component known not to be 0 (< or <= 0); short components against 0.5 where they
  are tiny; the window's wrap for i == 0 (the same column) and column > size (cannot be reached).
- The decorator index -2 for -1 (both past the set's end as unsigned).

Run 1 (642): 477 caught, 165 survived. New cases for 97 (the rest equivalent): the material's
log precision; the direction's two randoms; a diagonal box; the seed off z; a bend first in the
list and one not in it; Follow's sub indices at their edges, with shifts in, a far jump with a
shift, a one-cell grid, exactly 0 and under 0.5 positions, a 10-cell move where shift - origin
equals the cell; the cars off the grid's centre; the wheel's point and the tracks' middle probed
with rings of models (0.49 / 0.55 / 0.61 m) for every short direction and a square of 1.5; the
window's edges and its wrap below 0; heights in Bend; sets and decorators just past the end; a
spring taken on close; the move exactly along the model and 0.3 rad off it; short facings; the
crouch's radii, its alpha at rest, the fade's clamp at 1.05, the move's side (fading or not); a
bend's direction of square 1.5 and its short forms. TakeModel and Place take the unused seed
again (as the original's arguments). Run 2 (574): 571 caught; one more case (the 10-cell move).
The full rerun (573): all caught.
"""
